CHRoulette
Copyright 2026 bateske

From CHBlackjack (https://github.com/bateske/CHBlackjack, Apache-2.0): the
input and frame pacing (now in the CHGame library,
platform/board/arduino/CHGame/libraries/CHGame/src/chgame/Input.*), palette, drawing, outlined
lettering, effects, sound sequencer, flash saving, debug protocol, the PC
simulator and tools, the table's wall and rail, the chips, the croupier
(the dealer from CHBlackjack's tables, with his expressions) and the
end-screen lettering, adapted here. Two tunes (VICTORY and BROKE) are
CHBlackjack's.

CHBlackjack is a derivative of "Blackjack" for the Arduboy by Press Play On
Tape - Simon Holmes (filmote), code, and Stephane C (vampirics), art
(https://github.com/Press-Play-On-Tape/Blackjack, Apache-2.0). The croupier
is Press Play On Tape's dealer, recoloured and retouched by hand; the "YOU
WON THE BANK" and "YOU ARE BROKE" lettering and the 3x5 pixel font in the
CHGame library (platform/board/arduino/CHGame/libraries/CHGame/src/chgame/Draw.cpp) are Press
Play On Tape's.

From CHChess (https://github.com/bateske/CHChess, Apache-2.0): the pointing
glove, the nearest-in-direction navigation, the word plate, the soft clock
ticks and the shake routine.

Everything else - the betting layout, the wheel and its renderer, the ball
and its landing solver, the rules, the "Roulette" lettering, the title tune
and the presentation - is new, under the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE).
